              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\frac{2+\\sqrt3}{\\sqrt2+\\sqrt{2+\\sqrt3}}-\\frac{2-\\sqrt3}{\\sqrt2-\\sqrt{2-\\sqrt3}}=\\sqrt{\\frac23}.",
                  "display": true
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt{\\dfrac23}$.\n\nUse $\\sqrt{4+2\\sqrt3}=1+\\sqrt3$ and $\\sqrt{4-2\\sqrt3}=\\sqrt3-1$ after multiplying each fraction by $\\frac{\\sqrt2}{\\sqrt2}$.",
          "worked": "Since $(\\sqrt3-1)^2=4-2\\sqrt3$ and $\\sqrt3-1>0$, $\\sqrt{4-2\\sqrt3}=\\sqrt3-1$. Let $E$ denote the left-hand side.\n$$\\begin{align*}E&=\\frac{\\sqrt2(2+\\sqrt3)}{2+\\sqrt{4+2\\sqrt3}}-\\frac{\\sqrt2(2-\\sqrt3)}{2-\\sqrt{4-2\\sqrt3}}\\\\E&=\\sqrt2\\left(\\frac{2+\\sqrt3}{3+\\sqrt3}-\\frac{2-\\sqrt3}{3-\\sqrt3}\\right)\\\\E&=\\sqrt2\\left(\\frac{(2+\\sqrt3)(3-\\sqrt3)-(2-\\sqrt3)(3+\\sqrt3)}{9-3}\\right)\\\\E&=\\sqrt2\\left(\\frac{(3+\\sqrt3)-(3-\\sqrt3)}6\\right)\\\\E&=\\frac{\\sqrt6}3\\\\E&=\\sqrt{\\frac23}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      }
    ]
